# Frontend TypeScript Guidelines

## Stack conventions
- Use React + TypeScript patterns consistent with existing `frontend/src`.
- Keep formatting Prettier-compatible (`singleQuote: true`, no semicolons, width 80).
- Respect ESLint setup from `frontend/eslint.config.js`.

## Component patterns
- Keep components focused; move non-UI logic into helpers/hooks when complexity grows.
- Prefer explicit prop types/interfaces over implicit `any`.
- Avoid deeply nested conditional rendering; extract small subcomponents when needed.

## Data and API usage
- Reuse shared API integration points (e.g. `frontend/src/api.ts`) instead of ad-hoc fetch logic.
- Keep network error handling and loading states explicit in UI flows.

## UX and performance
- Preserve current UX behaviors (search responsiveness, keyboard interactions, mobile handling).
- Avoid introducing unnecessary rerenders; memoize only when profiling/clear benefit justifies it.

## Tests and validation
- For meaningful UI behavior changes, include a verification plan (manual steps or automated tests).
- Run lint/build checks before finalizing changes.
